# Karpathy Coding Guidelines

## 1. Think Before Coding
- State assumptions explicitly. If uncertain, ask.
- Surface tradeoffs and simpler alternatives. Push back on overengineering.

## 2. Simplicity First
- Minimum code that solves the problem. Nothing speculative.
- No unrequested abstractions, configurability, or premature optimizations.
- If 200 lines could be 50, rewrite it.

## 3. Surgical Changes
- Touch only what you must. Don't touch unrelated formatting or code.
- Clean up only your own mess.

## 4. Goal-Driven Execution
- Define clear success criteria and verify with tests or builds.
